IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `whsact-dates`
IMPORT `whsact-claims`

-- Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (ACT) -- worked cases for the claims questions in whsact-claims.l4.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run (the Schedule 4 amounts worked with a calculator from table 4.1 and 4.2, the
-- s 4.4 formula and the s 4.5 rounding); none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- (c) Australian Capital Territory. Used under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names`

`affected` MEANS `I am the person affected by the contravention`
`representative` MEANS `I am a representative authorised by the person affected`
`discriminated` MEANS `the person I sue engaged in discriminatory conduct against me (s 112 (2) (a))`
`procured` MEANS `the person I sue requested, instructed, induced, encouraged, authorised or assisted someone else to engage in discriminatory conduct against me (s 112 (2) (b))`
`coercion` MEANS `the person I sue coerced or induced, or tried to, about powers, functions or roles under the Act (s 108, s 112 (2) (c))`
`dismissed` MEANS `I was dismissed`
`nothing done` MEANS `none of these things was done`
`raised a concern` MEANS `I raise, raised or propose to raise a work health and safety issue or concern with the business, an inspector, a WHS entry permit-holder, a health and safety representative or committee member, another worker, or another person with a duty, power or function under the Act`
`an HSR` MEANS `I am, was or propose to be a health and safety representative or committee member`
`no circumstance` MEANS `none of these is true of me`

`ORDERS` MEANS `the court may make orders against the person (s 112 (2)); see the question on which orders`
`NOT FOR A PROHIBITED REASON` MEANS `no: the conduct was not discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason that was a substantial reason for it (s 112 (2), (4)) (the text's no)`
`REBUTTED` MEANS `no: the person sued proved, on the balance of probabilities, that the prohibited reason was not a substantial reason (s 113 (2)) (the text's no)`
`DEFENCE` MEANS `no: the person sued proved the defence that the conduct was reasonable and a substantial reason for it was to comply with the WHS laws (s 113 (3)) (the text's no)`
`NO COERCION` MEANS `no: there was no coercion or inducement contrary to s 108 (s 112 (2) (c)) (the text's no)`
`EMERGENCY` MEANS `no: a reasonable direction by a police officer or emergency services worker in an emergency is not coercion (s 108 (3)) (the text's no)`
`S111 ALREADY` MEANS `no: a s 111 order was already made in a prosecution for the same conduct (s 114 (3)) (the text's no)`
`NOT ELIGIBLE` MEANS `s 112 lets an affected person or their authorised representative apply; it says nothing of others (NOTHING-kind)`

`employee` MEANS `I am, or was, an employee`
`prospective` MEANS `I am a prospective employee`
`contractor` MEANS `I am, or was, a worker other than an employee (for example a contractor or volunteer)`
`INJUNCTION` MEANS `an injunction, from the Supreme Court (s 112 (1) (a), (3) (a))`
`COMPENSATION` MEANS `compensation the court considers appropriate, to be paid within a period the court specifies (s 112 (3) (b))`
`REINSTATEMENT` MEANS `reinstatement or re-employment in your former position or, if it is not available, a similar position (s 112 (3) (c) (i))`
`EMPLOYMENT` MEANS `employment in the position you applied for or a similar position (s 112 (3) (c) (ii))`
`OTHER ORDER` MEANS `any other order the court considers appropriate (s 112 (3) (d))`
`C COMPENSATION` MEANS `compensation in the criminal proceeding, to be paid within a period the court specifies (s 111 (a))`
`C REINSTATEMENT` MEANS `reinstatement or re-employment in your former position or a similar position, in the criminal proceeding (s 111 (b) (i))`
`C EMPLOYMENT` MEANS `employment in the position you applied for or a similar position, in the criminal proceeding (s 111 (b) (ii))`

`S115 OK` MEANS `s 115 does not stop you on these facts`
`S115 A` MEANS `you cannot commence the proceeding while your proceeding, application or complaint about the same matter under a Commonwealth or State law has not been withdrawn (s 115 (a)) (the text's no)`
`S115 C` MEANS `you cannot commence or continue the proceeding, because you failed in a proceeding, application or complaint about the same matter under a Commonwealth or State law (s 115 (c)) (the text's no)`

`IN TIME` MEANS `in time: commenced not more than 1 year after you knew or ought to have known the cause of action accrued (s 113 (1))`
`STILL IN TIME` MEANS `not yet commenced, and still in time (s 113 (1))`
`OUT OF TIME` MEANS `out of time: more than 1 year after you knew or ought to have known the cause of action accrued (s 113 (1)) (the text's no)`

`TERRITORY PAYS` MEANS `yes: you may claim compensation from the Territory, in a court of competent jurisdiction or in a prosecution brought against you under this Act, and the court may order it (s 184)`
`NOT JUST` MEANS `you may claim (s 184 (1)), but the court may not order compensation, because it is not satisfied it is just (s 184 (3)) (the text's no)`
`NOT ENTRY` MEANS `no: s 184 gives no claim, as your loss or expense was not caused by an inspector's exercise of an entry power (the text's no: its "if" fails)`

`improvement notice` MEANS `the issue of an improvement notice (s 191)`
`prohibition notice` MEANS `the issue of a prohibition notice (s 195)`
`PIN review` MEANS `an inspector's decision on review of a provisional improvement notice (s 102)`
`forfeiture` MEANS `the forfeiture of a seized thing (s 179)`
`other decision` MEANS `another decision (training, entry permits, or under the Regulation)`
`REVIEW AS WORKER` MEANS `yes: as a worker whose interests are affected by the decision, you are an eligible person (s 223, table 223)`
`REVIEW AS ENTITLED` MEANS `yes: as the person entitled to the seized thing, you are an eligible person (s 223, table 223)`
`NO REVIEW` MEANS `no: table 223 does not make you an eligible person for this decision (the text's no)`
`REVIEW NOT ENCODED` MEANS `table 223 makes a worker an eligible person only for the decisions it names; this one is not encoded as one, and may be prescribed by the Regulation (item 15, not deposited) (NOTHING-kind)`
`not by regulator` MEANS `the decision, not made by the regulator or a delegate of the regulator`
`by regulator` MEANS `the decision, made by the regulator or a delegate of the regulator`
`on internal review` MEANS `the decision made (or taken to have been made) on internal review`
`INTERNAL` MEANS `internal review: apply to the regulator (s 224)`
`EXTERNAL` MEANS `external review: apply to the ACAT (s 229)`
`STAYED` MEANS `stayed: your application for internal review stays the decision (s 228 (1))`
`STAYED BY REVIEWER` MEANS `stayed: the reviewer decided to stay it (s 228 (2))`
`STAYED BY DEFAULT` MEANS `stayed: the reviewer did not decide your application for a stay within 1 working day, so is taken to have granted it (s 228 (5))`
`STAY REFUSED` MEANS `not stayed: the reviewer refused your application for a stay within 1 working day (s 228 (2), (4))`
`NOT STAYED UNLESS` MEANS `not stayed unless the reviewer stays it on its own initiative (s 228 (2), (3)); you may apply for a stay`

`what happened` MEANS `from what happened: I reasonably consider it was a category 1 or category 2 offence`
`coronial` MEANS `from a coronial report, inquiry or inquest: I reasonably consider a category 1 or category 2 offence was committed`
`REQ IN TIME` MEANS `in time: you may make the written request to the regulator on this day (s 231 (1A), (1B))`
`REQ TOO EARLY` MEANS `too early: a request on what happened may be made only from 6 months after it happened (s 231 (1B) (a)) (the text's no)`
`REQ TOO LATE` MEANS `too late: the time for the request has passed (s 231 (1B)) (the text's no)`
`REQ PROSECUTED` MEANS `s 231 does not apply: a prosecution has been brought (the text's no: its "if" fails)`
`REQ NO OFFENCE` MEANS `s 231 does not apply: you do not reasonably consider a category 1 or category 2 offence was committed (the text's no: its "if" fails)`
`ANSWER IN TIME` MEANS `in time: the regulator advised you in writing within 3 months after receiving your request (s 231 (2))`
`ANSWER NOT YET` MEANS `not yet advised, and the 3 months have not run out (s 231 (2))`
`ANSWER LATE` MEANS `late: the regulator did not advise you in writing within 3 months after receiving your request (s 231 (2))`

`PROSECUTE OK` MEANS `yes: within the limitation period (s 232 (1))`
`PROSECUTE WITH LEAVE` MEANS `yes, with the court's leave, which it gives because it is in the interests of justice (s 232 (2), (3))`
`PROSECUTE NO` MEANS `no: the limitation period has ended and the court will not give leave, not being satisfied it is in the interests of justice (s 232 (3)) (the text's no)`
`PROSECUTE IM` MEANS `s 232 does not apply to industrial manslaughter; this Act sets no time limit for it (NOTHING-kind)`

`IM YES` MEANS `on these facts the elements of industrial manslaughter are made out (s 34A (1)); maximum penalty 20 years imprisonment for an individual, $18 000 000 for a body corporate`
`IM NO` MEANS `not industrial manslaughter on these facts (the text's no: an element of s 34A (1) is missing); a category 1 or 2 offence may still be found instead (s 34B)`

`IM` MEANS `industrial manslaughter (s 34A)`
`cat 1` MEANS `category 1: reckless or negligent exposure to a risk of death or serious injury (s 31)`
`cat 2` MEANS `category 2: failure to comply with a health and safety duty exposing someone to a risk of death or serious injury (s 32)`
`cat 3` MEANS `category 3: failure to comply with a health and safety duty (s 33)`
`tier A` MEANS `discriminatory conduct, or requesting or assisting it, coercion or misrepresentation (ss 104, 107, 108, 109: tier A)`
`tier D` MEANS `failing to notify the regulator of a notifiable incident, or to preserve the incident site (ss 38 (1), 39: tier D)`
`tier F` MEANS `charging a worker for anything done or provided for work health and safety (s 273: tier F)`
`a PCBU individual` MEANS `an individual who conducts the business or undertaking, or is an officer of it`
`other individual` MEANS `another individual (for example a worker)`
`a company` MEANS `a body corporate`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

§ `Part 6 -- s 105, s 106`

#ASSERT `s 105 -- is it discriminatory conduct` `dismissed`
#ASSERT `s 105 -- is it discriminatory conduct` `a commercial arrangement with me was terminated`
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 105 -- is it discriminatory conduct` `nothing done`))
#ASSERT `s 106 -- was it for a prohibited reason` `raised a concern` TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 106 -- was it for a prohibited reason` `raised a concern` FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 106 -- was it for a prohibited reason` `no circumstance` TRUE))

§ `Part 6 -- s 112 and s 113: can the court make orders`

-- A worker dismissed for raising a safety concern; the employer neither rebuts nor proves the defence.
#ASSERT `s 112 -- can the court make orders for me` `affected` `discriminated` `dismissed` `raised a concern` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ORDERS`
-- The union official authorised by the worker applies instead.
#ASSERT `s 112 -- can the court make orders for me` `representative` `discriminated` `dismissed` `raised a concern` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ORDERS`
-- A stranger to the matter.
#ASSERT `s 112 -- can the court make orders for me` `neither` `discriminated` `dismissed` `raised a concern` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT ELIGIBLE`
-- The employer proves the concern was not a substantial reason (s 113 (2)).
#ASSERT `s 112 -- can the court make orders for me` `affected` `discriminated` `dismissed` `raised a concern` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `REBUTTED`
-- The employer proves both limbs of the s 113 (3) defence; and only one limb.
#ASSERT `s 112 -- can the court make orders for me` `affected` `discriminated` `dismissed` `raised a concern` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `DEFENCE`
#ASSERT `s 112 -- can the court make orders for me` `affected` `discriminated` `dismissed` `raised a concern` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ORDERS`
-- Nothing within s 105 was done; and no prohibited reason alleged.
#ASSERT `s 112 -- can the court make orders for me` `affected` `discriminated` `nothing done` `raised a concern` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT FOR A PROHIBITED REASON`
#ASSERT `s 112 -- can the court make orders for me` `affected` `discriminated` `dismissed` `no circumstance` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT FOR A PROHIBITED REASON`
-- A manager who told the supervisor to sack the HSR (s 112 (2) (b)).
#ASSERT `s 112 -- can the court make orders for me` `affected` `procured` `dismissed` `an HSR` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ORDERS`
-- A s 111 order was already made in the prosecution for the same conduct (s 114 (3)).
#ASSERT `s 112 -- can the court make orders for me` `affected` `discriminated` `dismissed` `raised a concern` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `S111 ALREADY`
-- Coercion: threatened with loss of shifts unless the HSR stops issuing notices; none; an emergency direction.
#ASSERT `s 112 -- can the court make orders for me` `affected` `coercion` `nothing done` `no circumstance` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ORDERS`
#ASSERT `s 112 -- can the court make orders for me` `affected` `coercion` `nothing done` `no circumstance` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NO COERCION`
#ASSERT `s 112 -- can the court make orders for me` `affected` `coercion` `nothing done` `no circumstance` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `EMERGENCY`
-- The coercion route is not barred by an earlier s 111 order (s 114 (3) covers only s 112 (2) (a) and (b)).
#ASSERT `s 112 -- can the court make orders for me` `affected` `coercion` `nothing done` `no circumstance` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `ORDERS`

§ `Part 6 -- s 112 (3) orders, s 115 (b)`

-- A dismissed employee.
#ASSERT `s 112 (3) -- which orders may the court make for me` `discriminated` `employee` FALSE EQUALS LIST `INJUNCTION`, `COMPENSATION`, `REINSTATEMENT`, `OTHER ORDER`
-- A rejected job applicant.
#ASSERT `s 112 (3) -- which orders may the court make for me` `discriminated` `prospective` FALSE EQUALS LIST `INJUNCTION`, `COMPENSATION`, `EMPLOYMENT`, `OTHER ORDER`
-- A contractor whose contract was ended: no reinstatement.
#ASSERT `s 112 (3) -- which orders may the court make for me` `discriminated` `contractor` FALSE EQUALS LIST `INJUNCTION`, `COMPENSATION`, `OTHER ORDER`
-- Against the person who procured the dismissal (s 112 (2) (b)): no reinstatement order.
#ASSERT `s 112 (3) -- which orders may the court make for me` `procured` `employee` FALSE EQUALS LIST `INJUNCTION`, `COMPENSATION`, `OTHER ORDER`
-- Already compensated under a Commonwealth law (s 115 (b)).
#ASSERT `s 112 (3) -- which orders may the court make for me` `discriminated` `employee` TRUE EQUALS LIST `INJUNCTION`, `REINSTATEMENT`, `OTHER ORDER`
-- Coercion: an injunction or another order, no compensation.
#ASSERT `s 112 (3) -- which orders may the court make for me` `coercion` `employee` FALSE EQUALS LIST `INJUNCTION`, `OTHER ORDER`

§ `Part 6 -- s 115 (a), (c)`

#ASSERT `s 115 -- does another claim stop me` `I have no other proceeding, application or complaint about the same matter under a Commonwealth or State law` EQUALS `S115 OK`
-- A pending general protections application under a Commonwealth law.
#ASSERT `s 115 -- does another claim stop me` `I commenced one under a Commonwealth or State law and it has not been withdrawn` EQUALS `S115 A`
#ASSERT `s 115 -- does another claim stop me` `I commenced one under a Commonwealth or State law and withdrew it` EQUALS `S115 OK`
#ASSERT `s 115 -- does another claim stop me` `I failed in one under a Commonwealth or State law, not about workers compensation` EQUALS `S115 C`
-- A failed workers compensation claim does not stop the s 112 proceeding.
#ASSERT `s 115 -- does another claim stop me` `I failed in one under a Commonwealth or State law about workers compensation` EQUALS `S115 OK`

§ `s 113 (1) -- 1 year to commence`

#ASSERT `s 113 (1) -- the last day to commence` (`d` 15 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 15 3 2027
#ASSERT `s 113 (1) -- the last day to commence` (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2025
-- Commenced on the last day, and the day after.
#ASSERT `s 113 (1) -- am I in time` (`d` 15 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 15 3 2027) (`d` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 113 (1) -- am I in time` (`d` 15 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 16 3 2027) (`d` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`
-- Commenced on the day of knowledge, and (fork F5) the day before it.
#ASSERT `s 113 (1) -- am I in time` (`d` 15 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 113 (1) -- am I in time` (`d` 15 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 14 3 2026) (`d` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `IN TIME`
-- From 29 February 2024: 28 February 2025 is the last day.
#ASSERT `s 113 (1) -- am I in time` (`d` 29 2 2024) TRUE (`d` 28 2 2025) (`d` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 113 (1) -- am I in time` (`d` 29 2 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`
-- Not commenced: today the last day, and the day after.
#ASSERT `s 113 (1) -- am I in time` (`d` 15 3 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 15 3 2027) EQUALS `STILL IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 113 (1) -- am I in time` (`d` 15 3 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 16 3 2027) EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`
-- The regulative rule alone: 365 days allowed; day 365 fulfils, day 366 breaches.
#ASSERT `commencing on this day is in time` 365 365
#ASSERT (NOT (`commencing on this day is in time` 365 366))

§ `s 111 and s 114 (2)`

-- The employer convicted under s 104; the dismissed employee.
#ASSERT `s 111 -- which orders may the criminal court make for me` TRUE TRUE `employee` FALSE EQUALS LIST `C COMPENSATION`, `C REINSTATEMENT`
#ASSERT `s 111 -- which orders may the criminal court make for me` TRUE TRUE `prospective` FALSE EQUALS LIST `C COMPENSATION`, `C EMPLOYMENT`
#ASSERT `s 111 -- which orders may the criminal court make for me` TRUE TRUE `contractor` FALSE EQUALS LIST `C COMPENSATION`
-- A s 112 order already made for the same conduct; no conviction; not the subject of the conduct.
#ASSERT `s 111 -- which orders may the criminal court make for me` TRUE TRUE `employee` TRUE EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `s 111 -- which orders may the criminal court make for me` FALSE TRUE `employee` FALSE EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `s 111 -- which orders may the criminal court make for me` TRUE FALSE `employee` FALSE EQUALS EMPTY

§ `s 184 -- Compensation from the Territory`

-- A door broken in a search under warrant.
#ASSERT `s 184 -- can I get compensation from the Territory` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `TERRITORY PAYS`
#ASSERT `s 184 -- can I get compensation from the Territory` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NOT JUST`
-- Loss from an improvement notice, not an entry power.
#ASSERT `s 184 -- can I get compensation from the Territory` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `NOT ENTRY`

§ `Part 12 -- Review`

#ASSERT `s 223 -- can I apply for review` `prohibition notice` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `REVIEW AS WORKER`
#ASSERT `s 223 -- can I apply for review` `PIN review` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `REVIEW AS WORKER`
#ASSERT `s 223 -- can I apply for review` `prohibition notice` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NO REVIEW`
#ASSERT `s 223 -- can I apply for review` `forfeiture` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `REVIEW AS ENTITLED`
#ASSERT `s 223 -- can I apply for review` `forfeiture` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NO REVIEW`
-- Return of a seized thing: a worker as such is not eligible; the person entitled to it is.
#ASSERT `s 223 -- can I apply for review` `a decision about returning a seized thing (s 180)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NO REVIEW`
#ASSERT `s 223 -- can I apply for review` `a decision about returning a seized thing (s 180)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `REVIEW AS ENTITLED`
#ASSERT `s 223 -- can I apply for review` `other decision` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `REVIEW NOT ENCODED`

#ASSERT `s 224 and s 229 -- which review do I apply for` `not by regulator` EQUALS `INTERNAL`
#ASSERT `s 224 and s 229 -- which review do I apply for` `by regulator` EQUALS `EXTERNAL`
#ASSERT `s 224 and s 229 -- which review do I apply for` `on internal review` EQUALS `EXTERNAL`

-- Internal review of an improvement notice noticed on 1 March 2026: compliance in 7 days (lesser: 8 March); in 30 days
-- (14 days: 15 March); in exactly 14 days (15 March); with 28 days allowed by the regulator (29 March).
#ASSERT `s 224 and s 229 -- the last day to apply for review` `not by regulator` `improvement notice` (`d` 1 3 2026) 7 0 FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `d` 8 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 224 and s 229 -- the last day to apply for review` `not by regulator` `improvement notice` (`d` 1 3 2026) 30 0 FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `d` 15 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 224 and s 229 -- the last day to apply for review` `not by regulator` `improvement notice` (`d` 1 3 2026) 14 0 FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `d` 15 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 224 and s 229 -- the last day to apply for review` `not by regulator` `improvement notice` (`d` 1 3 2026) 7 28 FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `d` 29 3 2026
-- A prohibition notice noticed on 25 December 2025: 14 days runs into the new year.
#ASSERT `s 224 and s 229 -- the last day to apply for review` `not by regulator` `prohibition notice` (`d` 25 12 2025) 7 0 FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `d` 8 1 2026
-- ACAT review: 14 days; 28 days for a forfeiture; 14 days after a statement of reasons the ACAT required.
#ASSERT `s 224 and s 229 -- the last day to apply for review` `on internal review` `improvement notice` (`d` 1 3 2026) 7 0 FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `d` 15 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 224 and s 229 -- the last day to apply for review` `by regulator` `forfeiture` (`d` 1 3 2026) 0 0 FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `d` 29 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 224 and s 229 -- the last day to apply for review` `on internal review` `prohibition notice` (`d` 1 3 2026) 0 0 TRUE (`d` 10 4 2026) EQUALS `d` 24 4 2026

-- Stays.
#ASSERT `s 228 -- is the decision stayed while it is reviewed` `improvement notice` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `STAYED`
#ASSERT `s 228 -- is the decision stayed while it is reviewed` `prohibition notice` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `STAYED BY REVIEWER`
#ASSERT `s 228 -- is the decision stayed while it is reviewed` `prohibition notice` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `STAYED BY DEFAULT`
#ASSERT `s 228 -- is the decision stayed while it is reviewed` `prohibition notice` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `STAY REFUSED`
#ASSERT `s 228 -- is the decision stayed while it is reviewed` `the issue of a non-disturbance notice (s 198)` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT STAYED UNLESS`

§ `s 231 -- Asking for a prosecution`

-- A fall on 10 January 2025: the window is 10 July 2025 to 10 July 2026.
#ASSERT `s 231 -- may I ask for a prosecution on this day` `what happened` FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 9 7 2025) EQUALS `REQ TOO EARLY`
#ASSERT `s 231 -- may I ask for a prosecution on this day` `what happened` FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 10 7 2025) EQUALS `REQ IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 231 -- may I ask for a prosecution on this day` `what happened` FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 10 7 2026) EQUALS `REQ IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 231 -- may I ask for a prosecution on this day` `what happened` FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 11 7 2026) EQUALS `REQ TOO LATE`
-- From 31 August 2024: 6 months is 28 February 2025, 18 months is 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `s 231 -- may I ask for a prosecution on this day` `what happened` FALSE (`d` 31 8 2024) (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 27 2 2025) EQUALS `REQ TOO EARLY`
#ASSERT `s 231 -- may I ask for a prosecution on this day` `what happened` FALSE (`d` 31 8 2024) (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 28 2 2025) EQUALS `REQ IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 231 -- may I ask for a prosecution on this day` `what happened` FALSE (`d` 31 8 2024) (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 28 2 2026) EQUALS `REQ IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 231 -- may I ask for a prosecution on this day` `what happened` FALSE (`d` 31 8 2024) (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `REQ TOO LATE`
-- An inquest ended 31 March 2026: 6 months is 30 September 2026; a request on the day the inquest ended is in time.
#ASSERT `s 231 -- may I ask for a prosecution on this day` `coronial` FALSE (`d` 10 1 2023) (`d` 31 3 2026) (`d` 31 3 2026) EQUALS `REQ IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 231 -- may I ask for a prosecution on this day` `coronial` FALSE (`d` 10 1 2023) (`d` 31 3 2026) (`d` 30 9 2026) EQUALS `REQ IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 231 -- may I ask for a prosecution on this day` `coronial` FALSE (`d` 10 1 2023) (`d` 31 3 2026) (`d` 1 10 2026) EQUALS `REQ TOO LATE`
-- A prosecution already brought; no basis.
#ASSERT `s 231 -- may I ask for a prosecution on this day` `what happened` TRUE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 10 9 2025) EQUALS `REQ PROSECUTED`
#ASSERT `s 231 -- may I ask for a prosecution on this day` `neither of these` FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 10 9 2025) EQUALS `REQ NO OFFENCE`

-- s 231 (2): received 30 November 2025; the last day is 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `s 231 (2) -- the last day for the regulator's answer` (`d` 30 11 2025) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `s 231 (2) -- did the regulator answer in time` (`d` 30 11 2025) TRUE (`d` 28 2 2026) (`d` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `ANSWER IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 231 (2) -- did the regulator answer in time` (`d` 30 11 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `ANSWER LATE`
#ASSERT `s 231 (2) -- did the regulator answer in time` (`d` 30 11 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 28 2 2026) EQUALS `ANSWER NOT YET`
#ASSERT `s 231 (2) -- did the regulator answer in time` (`d` 30 11 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `ANSWER LATE`
#ASSERT `advice on this day is in time` 90 90
#ASSERT (NOT (`advice on this day is in time` 90 91))

-- s 231 (3) (b): 1 month of the request; from 31 January, the end of February.
#ASSERT `s 231 (3) -- the last day for referral to the DPP` (`d` 31 1 2026) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `s 231 (3) -- the last day for referral to the DPP` (`d` 31 1 2024) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2024
#ASSERT `s 231 (3) -- the last day for referral to the DPP` (`d` 15 6 2026) EQUALS `d` 15 7 2026

§ `s 232 -- Limitation period for prosecutions`

-- Came to the regulator's notice 1 July 2024: 1 July 2026.
#ASSERT `s 232 -- the last day for a prosecution` FALSE (`d` 1 7 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (`d` 1 7 2026)
-- An inquest ended 1 December 2025 showing an offence: 1 December 2026 is later.
#ASSERT `s 232 -- the last day for a prosecution` FALSE (`d` 1 7 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 12 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (`d` 1 12 2026)
-- An inquest that ended earlier gives an earlier day: the 2-year period is the latest.
#ASSERT `s 232 -- the last day for a prosecution` FALSE (`d` 1 7 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (`d` 1 7 2026)
-- A WHS undertaking contravened on 2 June 2026: 2 December 2026, later still.
#ASSERT `s 232 -- the last day for a prosecution` FALSE (`d` 1 7 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 12 2025) TRUE (`d` 2 6 2026) EQUALS JUST (`d` 2 12 2026)
-- Industrial manslaughter: s 232 does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 232 -- the last day for a prosecution` TRUE (`d` 1 7 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 232 -- can they still be prosecuted` FALSE (`d` 1 7 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 7 2026) FALSE EQUALS `PROSECUTE OK`
#ASSERT `s 232 -- can they still be prosecuted` FALSE (`d` 1 7 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 2 7 2026) FALSE EQUALS `PROSECUTE NO`
#ASSERT `s 232 -- can they still be prosecuted` FALSE (`d` 1 7 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 2 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS `PROSECUTE WITH LEAVE`
#ASSERT `s 232 -- can they still be prosecuted` TRUE (`d` 1 7 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 2 7 2036) FALSE EQUALS `PROSECUTE IM`

§ `s 34A -- Industrial manslaughter`

-- A director whose decision to remove a guard breached the officer's duty and caused a worker's death, recklessly.
#ASSERT `s 34A -- could it be industrial manslaughter` TRUE TRUE TRUE `a worker died` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `IM YES`
-- A worker injured and dying weeks later; a member of the public killed.
#ASSERT `s 34A -- could it be industrial manslaughter` TRUE TRUE TRUE `a worker was injured and later died of the injury` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `IM YES`
#ASSERT `s 34A -- could it be industrial manslaughter` TRUE TRUE TRUE `another person died` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `IM YES`
-- Each element missing in turn.
#ASSERT `s 34A -- could it be industrial manslaughter` FALSE TRUE TRUE `a worker died` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `IM NO`
#ASSERT `s 34A -- could it be industrial manslaughter` TRUE FALSE TRUE `a worker died` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `IM NO`
#ASSERT `s 34A -- could it be industrial manslaughter` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a worker died` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `IM NO`
#ASSERT `s 34A -- could it be industrial manslaughter` TRUE TRUE TRUE `no one died` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `IM NO`
#ASSERT `s 34A -- could it be industrial manslaughter` TRUE TRUE TRUE `a worker died` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `IM NO`
#ASSERT `s 34A -- could it be industrial manslaughter` TRUE TRUE TRUE `a worker died` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `IM NO`

§ `Schedule 4 -- Maximum penalties`

-- Industrial manslaughter, body corporate: $18 000 000, not indexed. An individual: imprisonment only. Before 2024-25:
-- not answered.
#ASSERT `Schedule 4 -- the most the court can fine` `IM` `a company` 2025 150 123.9 EQUALS JUST 18000000
#ASSERT `Schedule 4 -- the most the court can fine` `IM` `a PCBU individual` 2025 150 123.9 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Schedule 4 -- the most the court can fine` `cat 1` `a company` 2023 137.4 123.9 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Category 1, body corporate, CPI 137.4 / 123.9: 10 425 000 x 137.4 / 123.9 = 11 560 895.88, to the nearest $1 000 =
-- $11 561 000.
#ASSERT `Schedule 4 -- the most the court can fine` `cat 1` `a company` 2024 137.4 123.9 EQUALS JUST 11561000
-- Category 1, individual conducting the business: 2 085 000 x 137.4 / 123.9 = 2 312 179.18 -> $2 312 000.
#ASSERT `Schedule 4 -- the most the court can fine` `cat 1` `a PCBU individual` 2024 137.4 123.9 EQUALS JUST 2312000
-- Category 2 and 3 with an index ratio of 1 (B = C): the table amounts.
#ASSERT `Schedule 4 -- the most the court can fine` `cat 2` `other individual` 2024 123.9 123.9 EQUALS JUST 209000
#ASSERT `Schedule 4 -- the most the court can fine` `cat 3` `a company` 2024 123.9 123.9 EQUALS JUST 700000
-- Tier A, an individual, CPI 140.7 / 123.9: 139 000 x 140.7 / 123.9 = 157 847.46 -> $158 000.
#ASSERT `Schedule 4 -- the most the court can fine` `tier A` `other individual` 2025 140.7 123.9 EQUALS JUST 158000
-- Tier F, individual: 7 000 x 137.4 / 123.9 = 7 762.71, under $10 000, to the nearest $100 = $7 800.
#ASSERT `Schedule 4 -- the most the court can fine` `tier F` `other individual` 2024 137.4 123.9 EQUALS JUST 7800
-- Rounding edges (s 4.5): 7 000 x 141 / 140 = 7 050, a $50 rounds down to $7 000; 7 000 x 7 051 / 7 000 = 7 051 -> $7 100;
-- 14 000 x 145 / 140 = 14 500, a $500 rounds down to $14 000; 14 000 x 145.01 / 140 = 14 501 -> $15 000;
-- 7 000 x 10 000 / 7 000 = exactly $10 000, unchanged.
#ASSERT `Schedule 4 -- the most the court can fine` `tier F` `other individual` 2024 141 140 EQUALS JUST 7000
#ASSERT `Schedule 4 -- the most the court can fine` `tier F` `other individual` 2024 7051 7000 EQUALS JUST 7100
#ASSERT `Schedule 4 -- the most the court can fine` `tier D` `a PCBU individual` 2024 145 140 EQUALS JUST 14000
#ASSERT `Schedule 4 -- the most the court can fine` `tier D` `a PCBU individual` 2024 145.01 140 EQUALS JUST 15000
#ASSERT `Schedule 4 -- the most the court can fine` `tier F` `other individual` 2024 10000 7000 EQUALS JUST 10000
-- Tier D, body corporate, ratio 1: $70 000.
#ASSERT `Schedule 4 -- the most the court can fine` `tier D` `a company` 2024 123.9 123.9 EQUALS JUST 70000

-- Imprisonment.
#ASSERT `the longest imprisonment in years` `IM` `a PCBU individual` EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `the longest imprisonment in years` `cat 1` `other individual` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `the longest imprisonment in years` `cat 2` `a PCBU individual` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the longest imprisonment in years` `IM` `a company` EQUALS 0
